cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use agent-trash-guard in your research or tooling, please cite it."
title: "agent-trash-guard: Recoverable-Delete Safety Net for Coding Agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bosch Rodriguez"
    given-names: "Rolando"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4896-1112"
    affiliation: "Hermes Labs"
version: "0.1.2"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/agent-trash-guard"
url: "https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/agent-trash-guard"
abstract: >
  agent-trash-guard is a safety net for coding-agent sessions: it intercepts
  permanent-delete shell commands (rm, unlink, shred, rmdir, find -delete,
  git clean -f) before they run and redirects them to a recoverable trash
  directory via the agent-trash CLI. It ships as one portable Agent Plugin
  with native pre-tool adapters for Claude Code, Codex CLI, and Gemini CLI,
  backed by a single detector and a canonical skill that teaches an agent the
  trash workflow. It has no dependencies beyond Python 3 (stdlib only) and
  bash.
keywords:
  - "coding agents"
  - "AI safety"
  - "recoverable deletion"
  - "pre-tool hooks"
  - "Claude Code"
  - "Codex CLI"
  - "Gemini CLI"
